  "_coats": "COATS (species.js coatDef, picked by the seed; creatures.js dressed): each a colour table over the horse's own, written out whole (the body, its darker back and paler flank, the muzzle, ears, legs, mane and tail) -- bay (its own), chestnut, black, grey, dun (the dark dorsal stripe: its `back`), chestnut with a blaze and white stockings, bay with white socks, dark bay, dapple grey, palomino, buckskin, flaxen chestnut, piebald, appaloosa. THE LEGS: `sock` is the leg from the knee down (a bay's black points; white: stockings), `pastern` the fetlock and pastern alone (white socks), each falling back to the one above. THE PARAMS a coat may set: `blaze` (a white stripe down the face, in `blaze`), `pinto` (black patches over a white coat: coatpat.js 47 `pinto`), `spotted` (an appaloosa's leopard spots: 21 `dots`), `dapple` (a dapple grey's dapples: 46 `dapple`) -- the patterns are the body's shapes' `pat`, gated on them",
  "print": "hoof",
